From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Claude Opus 5.5" <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 10:42:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 07/39] Spectator mode: the real mouse and keyboard don't reach
 the viewer

IbashoSpectator (on at every launch, not saved; IbashoAgent spectator {on}):
LLWindowWin32 drops OS mouse, keyboard, IME and raw-input messages, answers
client-area WM_MOUSEACTIVATE with MA_NOACTIVATE, keeps the pointer an arrow,
and never moves, hides, clips or captures the real cursor or takes focus
(show, bringToFront, focusClient, file drops). LEAP input calls the window
callbacks directly, so it works as before; the window's cursor position
follows LEAP mouse events, and is parked off-window when the mode turns on.
---
